    "portfolio.belizian-boat.title": "A Belizian Boat",
    "portfolio.belizian-boat.meta": "Acrylic · 2018",
    "portfolio.belizian-boat.alt": "A Belizian Boat: a small white motorboat tied to a wooden dock on dark water, under a cloudy sky.",
    "portfolio.rabbit-head-screw.title": "Rabbit Head Screw",
    "portfolio.rabbit-head-screw.meta": "Graphite, Oil Pastel · 2019",
    "portfolio.rabbit-head-screw.note": "This is a set of shackles holding a prisoner, the old wooden kind, with nails driven into it. The head of one of the nails is a rabbit. Whether you want to set the prisoner free or bring him to justice, you have to strike the rabbit or pull it out.",
    "portfolio.rabbit-head-screw.alt": "Rabbit Head Screw: a hammer raised over a screw whose head is a white rabbit.",
    "portfolio.heron.title": "Heron",
    "portfolio.heron.meta": "Graphite · 2018",
    "portfolio.heron.alt": "Heron: a graphite drawing of a heron with its head tucked into its feathers, among large leaves.",
    "portfolio.intolerance.title": "Intolerance",
    "portfolio.intolerance.meta": "Color pencil, Oil Pastel · 2019",
    "portfolio.intolerance.alt": "Intolerance: a green-faced girl with blue hair in a hallway lined with orange lockers, with brightly colored figures behind her.",
    "portfolio.mirror-girl.title": "Mirror Girl",
    "portfolio.mirror-girl.meta": "Acrylic · 2019",
    "portfolio.mirror-girl.note": "This is a girl whose skin has mirror magic. When people stare at her and judge her, her skin turns into a mirror. Then they can no longer judge her. All they can see in the mirror is themselves.",
    "portfolio.mirror-girl.alt": "Mirror Girl: a woman lying with her eyes closed. Patches of her skin are mirrors that reflect the eyes of the people staring at her.",
    "portfolio.mom.title": "Mom",
    "portfolio.mom.meta": "Oil Pastel · 2019",
    "portfolio.mom.alt": "Mom: a woman in a green top sits on a stool at a table on a brightly colored terrace with arches behind her.",
    "portfolio.dad.title": "Dad",
    "portfolio.dad.meta": "Acrylic · 2019",
    "portfolio.dad.alt": "Dad: a man’s face built from patches of color on a blue background, with a striped snake beside him and a rubber duck in a top hat on his head.",
    "portfolio.more-of-the-same-dad.title": "More of the Same Dad",
    "portfolio.more-of-the-same-dad.meta": "Acrylic · 2020",
    "portfolio.more-of-the-same-dad.alt": "More of the Same Dad: a dark figure on a yellow ground. The face is drawn in white lines inside a red circle, with birds on wires above and paper planes at each side.",
    "portfolio.photosynthesis.title": "Photosynthesis Grandpa and Me",
    "portfolio.photosynthesis.meta": "Acrylic · 2019",
    "portfolio.photosynthesis.note": "This is my grandpa. I grew up with him. My dad smoked, so for the sake of my health Grandpa wanted to clean the air and kept lots of flowers at home. So I made this wooden box. There is an LED light on top of my head, and when the box is closed, my light shines on the plants growing on Grandpa’s head.",
    "portfolio.photosynthesis.alt": "Photosynthesis Grandpa and Me: an open wooden box with a face painted inside each half, a young one on the left and an old one on the right with air plants growing from the top of his head.",
    "portfolio.aposematic.title": "Aposematic (Unfinished)",
    "portfolio.aposematic.meta": "Acrylic · 2019 – Present",
    "portfolio.aposematic.note": "I worked on this painting on and off for a long time and never managed to finish it. I probably never will, haha. It is about a concept from biology called aposematic coloration: bright colors can be a sign of poison, a warning. But that danger is also very beautiful, and fascinating.",
    "portfolio.aposematic.alt": "Aposematic (Unfinished): a woman in profile with bright eye makeup and a patterned snake coiled around her shoulders, on a black canvas standing on an easel.",
    "portfolio.digital-red.title": "Untitled",
    "portfolio.digital-red.meta": "Digital · 2020",
    "portfolio.digital-red.alt": "Untitled digital painting: a girl with twin buns tied with red ribbons, on a red background.",
    "portfolio.digital-alley.title": "Untitled",
    "portfolio.digital-alley.meta": "Digital · 2020",
    "portfolio.digital-alley.alt": "Untitled digital painting: a girl in a red floral kimono crouches to pet an orange cat in a dim alley.",
    "portfolio.digital-lamp.title": "Untitled",
    "portfolio.digital-lamp.meta": "Digital · 2020",
    "portfolio.digital-lamp.alt": "Untitled digital drawing in grey: a boy in a T-shirt. In a square on his chest, a lamp shines over a sleeping cat.",
    "portfolio.nezha.title": "NeZha Collection",
    "portfolio.nezha.meta": "Digital · 2020",
    "portfolio.nezha.note": "A series of fan art of The Legend of Nezha, a cartoon I loved as a child.",
    "portfolio.knight-dairy.title": "Knight Dairy",
    "portfolio.knight-dairy.meta": "2018",
    "portfolio.knight-dairy.note": "This one is about my biology teacher. I loved biology class because he was a wonderful teacher.",
    "portfolio.knight-dairy.alt": "Knight Dairy: a hand-drawn one-page comic. Boss Knight orders yogurt, cheese and latte, and cartoon cows, milk bottles, a splicesome and a proteasome carry out the order.",
    "portfolio.neurotic-cat.title": "The Neurotic Cat",
    "portfolio.neurotic-cat.meta": "A little book · 4 chapters · 2018",
    "portfolio.neurotic-cat.note": "A series of short comics about a cat named Neuro, who loves watching humans and poking fun at them. There are four little stories in the series.",
    "portfolio.rabbit.title": "Xiaoman",
    "portfolio.rabbit.alt": "Xiaoman: a fluffy lop-eared rabbit in grey-violet and cream, on a pale grey ground.",
    "portfolio.cat-plate.title": "Stray cat",
    "portfolio.cat-plate.alt": "Stray cat: a cat’s head in profile, painted in brown, ochre and blue on a cream plate.",
    "portfolio.tools.title": "Grandpa's Toolbox",
    "portfolio.tools.meta": "Pen · 2018",
    "portfolio.tools.note": "This is the toolbox my grandpa used for gardening. It is full of all sorts of odd little tools he collected over the years. I love it. As a child I often worked alongside him, holding tools that didn’t quite fit my hands, trying to solve some gardening problem and clumsily puzzling over it for a whole afternoon. It made me so happy.",
    "portfolio.tools.alt": "Grandpa’s Toolbox: a blue pen drawing of tools lying in a wooden box, among them scissors, a wrench, a brush and pliers.",
    "portfolio.pavilion.title": "Long Tan Lake Park",
    "portfolio.pavilion.meta": "Pen · Oct 25, 2017",
    "portfolio.pavilion.note": "This is the park I went to with my grandpa every weekend when I was little. Grandpa practiced tai chi there while I fed the stray cats and the ducks. Someone sold mantou (steamed buns) at the gate, and every time we bought two yuan’s worth. Then Grandpa did his tai chi and I fed the ducks and the pigeons. For the cats, I brought milk and beef from home. We spent the whole morning in the park, and then Grandpa and I went to eat baozi.",
    "portfolio.pavilion.alt": "Long Tan Lake Park: a pen drawing of a two-tiered pavilion on a stone bridge beside the water, with bare branches and willows around it.",
    "portfolio.iguana.title": "Reptile",
    "portfolio.iguana.meta": "2017",
    "portfolio.iguana.alt": "Reptile: an iguana’s head and neck drawn in fine white lines on black.",
